The FTIR spectra of   PLGA/chitosan, Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan/Paclitaxel nanofibers are illustrated in Fig.5. For PLGA/chitosan nanofibers, the observed bonds at $3200{-}3600\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , 2924 $\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , $2848~\mathrm{{cm}^{-1}}$ , $1741~\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , $1440\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , $1240\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ and $1033~\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ were assigned to O-H/N-H, asymmetric $\mathrm{CH}_{2}$ , symmetric $\mathrm{CH}_{2}$ stretching, $\scriptstyle\mathbf{C=O}$ , C–H,  C–O–C and C-O stretching of PLGA and chitosan. The bonds at the wave numbers of $895~\mathrm{{cm}^{-1}}$ , $1547\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , $1628~\mathrm{{cm}^{-1}}$ and $1669\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ were related to the saccharide groups, N–H bending, amide I stretching and amide II bending in the chitosan matrix. For Paclitaxel, the observed peaks at $3095\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , $770\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ and $708\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ were attributed to the absorbance bands of $\mathrm{C}{\cdot}\mathrm{H}$ in the benzene ring of paclitaxel. The presence of peaks at $3630\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ $\mathrm{n}^{-1},1721\mathrm{cm}^{-1},1650\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ , $1245~\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ and $1078~\mathrm{{cm}^{-1}}$ were assigned to the O-H, $\scriptstyle\mathbf{C=O}$ , C-C, C-N and C-O groups in the paclitaxel structure [65].  The main peaks of both Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan nanofibers were detected in the FTIR spectrum of Paclitaxel loaded- PLGA/chitosan nanofibers.
