## 3.2 Drug loading efficiency, drug release and kinetic studies
The drug loading efficiency (DLE) and drug content of PLGA/chitosan/Paclitaxel, ZIF8/Paclitaxel, MIL-101/Paclitaxel, NaY/Paclitaxel, ZSM-5/Paclitaxel, and synthesized nanoparticles/Paclitaxel loaded- PLGA/chitosan nanofibers were investigated which results are presented in Table 1. As shown, the direct loading of Paclitaxel into the PLGA/chitosan nanofibers led to obtain the DLE of $95.5{\pm}0.5\%$ . The DLE of Paclitaxel in the NaY and ZSM-5 zeolites were found to be $36.2{\pm}1.1\%$ and $32.2{\pm}1.5\%$ , respectively. Although, the incorporation of hydrophobic Paclitaxel molecules into the hydrophobic ZSM-5 nanozeolites was easier than that of loading of Paclitaxel molecules into the hydrophilic NaY zeolite, the higher DLE was achieved for Paclitaxel molecules loaded-NaY zeolite due to its higher surface area compared with Paclitaxel loaded-ZSM-5 nanozeolite. Therefore, the higher surface area of nanozeolites was predominant mechanism for loading of Paclitaxel drug into the nanozeolites and the most of Paclitacel drugs have been accumulated on the zeolites surface. Furthermore, the presence of paclitaxel molecules on the surface of the zeolites may be attributed to precipitation of the drug molecules on the zeolites surface during mixing of drug and nanoparticles due to lower pore sizes of zeolite [66].  The DLE of ZIF-8/Paclitaxel, MIL-101/Paclitaxel was about $53.3{\pm}1.5\%$ and $45.2{\pm}1\%$ , respectively. The DLE of nanozeolites/Paclitaxel and NMOFs/ Paclitaxel was found to be higher than $80\%$ due to presence of non-attached-nanozeolites/Paclitaxel and NMOFs/ Paclitaxel on the nanofibers surface compared with DLE of PLGA/chitosan nanofibers $(95\%)$ . The higher DLE efficiency of nanofibers containing ZIF-8 NMOFs compared with other nanofibrous formulations could be attributed to the lower particle sizes of ZIF NMOFs and the better incorporation of NMOFs into the nanofibers.
