## 3.3 Cell viability
The cell viabilities of synthesized pristine Paclitaxel, PLGA/chitosan, PLGA/chitosan/zeolites, PLGA/chitosan/NMOFs, PLGA/chitosan/zeolites/Paclitaxel and
PLGA/chitosan/NMOFs/Paclitaxel toward LNCaP cancer cells and fibroblast normal cells are illustrated in Fig. 7. As shown, the cell viability percentage of fibroblast normal cells after treated with all samples were higher than $85\%$ which indicated the lower cytotoxicity of the synthesized carriers in normal cells and revealed the high biocompatibility of synthesized nanofibrous samples. The pure PLGA/chitosan nanofibers did not show any significant effect on the LNCaP cancer cells death. The hydrophilic nanofibrous samples including PLGA/chitosan/ Paclitaxel, PLGA/chitosan/NaY/ Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan/MIL-101/ Paclitaxel could be efficiently killed the pure Paclitaxel LNCaP cells during $72\mathrm{{h}}$ incubation time compared with pristine Paclitaxel due to relative linear release of Paclitaxel during $72\mathrm{{h}}$ (Fig.7c). Whereas, the release rate of Paclitaxel from PLGA/chitosan/ZSM-5/ Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8/ Paclitaxel was increased between 72 and $120\mathrm{h}$ compared with release rate of paclitaxel before 72 h which resulted in the maximum killing of  LNCaP cells $(82\%)$ after $120\mathrm{h}$ incubation time (Fig.7c). The higher cell killing of nanofibrous samples containing NMOFs compared with nanozeolites loaded-nanofibers could be attributed to the higher drug content in PLGA/chitosan/MIL-101/ Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8/ Paclitaxel nanofibrous samples.
Furthermore, the release of mineral nanoparticles existed in the zeolites structure and metals in the NMOFs particles structure could increase the cellular uptake which resulted in the higher cytotoxicity of MOFs/ Paclitaxel and zeolites/ Paclitaxel loaded-PLGA/chitosan nanofibers against LNCaP cancer cells death in comparison to cell viability of PLGA/chitosan/Paclitaxel nanofibers [67, 68].
\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*Fig.7\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*
The DAPI staining images of untreated LNCaP cells and cells treated with PLGA/chitosan, PLGA/chitosan/Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8/Paclitaxel after $120\mathrm{h}$ incubation time results are illustrated in Fig. 8. As shown, the cells treated with PLGA/chitosan nanofibers did not show any chromatin degradation compared with the untreated cells (control) and the similar morphologies were observed for untreated LNCaP cells and cells treated with PLGA/chitosan nanofibers. Whereas, for cells treated with PLGA/chitosan/Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan/ZIF8/Paclitaxel nanofibers, the nuclear fragmentation in their chromatin was observed and the DAPI dye intensity was decreased which demonstrated the LNCaP cells death with apoptotic effects. Furthermore, the higher fragmentized nuclei of cells treated with PLGA/chitosan/ZIF8/Paclitaxel nanofibers in comparison to PLGA/chitosan/ Paclitaxel indicated the synergic effects of ZIF-8 NMOFs and Paclitaxel anticancer drug on the enhancement of the apoptotic nuclei.
\*\*\*\*\*\*\*Fig.8\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*
The in vivo experiments were performed on the LNCaP-tumor-bearing mice which results are illustrated in Fig.9. As shown, there was a steady increase in tumor volume in all groups and the pure PBS and nanofibers without drug did not repress the fast tumor growth. Whereas, the nanofibers containing zeolites, MOF and Paclitaxel could inhibit the growth rate of the tumor. A minimum growth of tumor volume was obtained in the PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8/ Paclitaxel groups after 20 days which could be attributed to the slower release of Paclitaxel from PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8/ Paclitaxel nanofibers compared with other nanofibrous formulations. The improvement of the antitumor efficacy of Paclitaxel in vivo was attributed to the synergistic chemotherapy effect of ZIF-8 NMOF /Paclitaxel and nanofibers in inhibiting of tumor cells as well as good the good biocompatibility of synthesized nanofibrous carrier as conformed by in vitro experiments.
\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*Fig.9\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*\*
## 4. Conclusion
The hydrophilic Y zeolite, hydrophobic ZSM-5 zeolite, MIL-101 NMOF and ZIF-8 NMOF were incorporated into the PLGA/chitosan nanofibers for the controlled release of Paclitaxel and the prostate cancer treatment in vitro and in vivo. The XRD patterns of nanoparticles revealed a successful synthesis of MIL-101, ZIF-8 NMOFs and ZSM-5, NaY nanozeolites. The average particle size of MIL-101, ZIF-8 NMOFs, NaY and ZSM-5 nanozeolites were found to be $55\mathrm{nm}$ , $45\mathrm{nm}$ , 95 and $75\mathrm{nm}$ , respectively. The average diameter of PLGA/chitosan/ MIL-101- /Paclitaxel, PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8-/Paclitaxel, PLGA/chitosan/NaY-/Paclitaxel and PLGA/chitosan/ZSM-5-/Paclitaxel were found to be 340, 370, 325 and $310\mathrm{nm}$ , respectively. The FTIR spectrum of nanofibers containing Paclitaxel confirmed the presence of Paclitaxel molecules in the PLGA/chitosan nanofibrous matrix. The BET surface area of synthesized NaY nanozeolite, ZSM-5 nanozeolite, ZIF-8 NMOFs and MIL-101 NMOFs were found to be 413.2, 335.1, 812.3 and $1875\mathrm{m}^{2}.\mathrm{g}^{-1}$ , respectively. The water contact angle of synthesized PLGA/chitosan, MIL-101/Paclitaxel, ZIF-8/Paclitaxel, NaY/Paclitaxel and ZSM-5/Paclitaxel loaded- PLGA/chitosan nanofibers were found to be $45{\pm}3.5^{\circ}$ , $26{\pm}4.2^{\circ}$ , $65{\pm}5.3^{\circ}$ , $31{\pm}5.5^{\circ}$ and
$86{\pm}4.5^{\circ}$ , respectively. The drug loading efficiency of  NaY/Paclitaxel, ZSM-5/Paclitaxel, of ZIF8/Paclitaxel, and MIL-101/Paclitaxel were found to be $36.2{\pm}1.1\%$ , $32.2{\pm}1.5\%$ , $53{\pm}1.5\%$ and $45\pm1\%$ , respectively. The drug release profiles indicated the higher drug release rate from all synthesized carriers under acidic pH compared with pH of 7.4. The slower release of Paclitaxel was obtained from using PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8 and PLGA/chitosan/ ZSM-5 nanofibers within 360 h, 480 h under acidic pH and 600 h, 720 h, under physiological $\mathrm{pH}$ , respectively. The the PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8/ Paclitaxel indicated the maximum cell killing of $86\%$ after $72\mathrm{{h}}$ . The flow cytometric assay indicated a more synergistic chemotherapy effect of nanofibers containing NMOF and Paclitaxel compared with nanozeolites/Paclitaxel loaded-nanofibers for apoptosis of LNCaP cancer cells. A minimum growth of tumor volume was obtained in the PLGA/chitosan/ZIF-8/ Paclitaxel groups after 20 days. The obtained results confirmed a better performance of anticancer drug loaded-hydrophobic NMOFs loaded-nanofibers compared with zeolites and hydrophilic NMOF loaded-nanofibers for controlled release of anticancer drug and treatment of cancers.
